{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via the cobbler orchestrator) submitted stitch task #5464 to implement srd070 requirements R6.1, R7.1, R8.1, and R9.1 for `cmd/fmt` (simple text formatter). The task requires:\n   - Implementing R6.1: Goal width (`-g GOAL` / `--goal=GOAL` flag, default 93% of width)\n   - Implementing R7.1: Word boundary breaking (break at spaces, not mid-word unless word exceeds max width)\n   - Implementing R8.1: Space collapsing (collapse multiple spaces to one, preserve two after sentence-ending punctuation)\n   - Implementing R9.1: Split-only mode (`-s` / `--split-only` splits long lines without joining short ones)\n   - Adding differential tests for all four requirements\n   - Ensuring `go build`, `go vet`, and `go test` all pass\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing against GNU reference binary `gfmt` via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Paragraph-based text formatting with configurable width and goal width\n   - Split-only mode vs. fill mode\n   - Sentence-ending punctuation detection (`.`, `!`, `?`) for double-space preservation\n   - Flag parsing (short `-w`, `-g`, `-s`, `-t`, `-u`, `-p` and long `--width=`, `--goal=`, etc.)\n   - The cobbler orchestrator manages git; no git commands allowed\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd070-fmt.yaml**\n     - Source of truth for all fmt requirements\n     - R6.1: \"-g GOAL or --goal=GOAL must set the goal line width. Lines are filled to approximately GOAL characters. Default goal is 93% of width.\"\n     - R7.1: \"Must break lines at word boundaries (spaces). Must not break in the middle of a word unless the word exceeds the maximum wid